xis of symmetry is $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082943 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14836" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082943 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y=-x^2+4x+1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082943 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4cf6319-af75-53c4-a5a8-87478b7c3fd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082943 #edb/ref 1074 "The vertex of the parabola lies on the axis of symmetry, so we will start by computing the axis of symmetry. \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=ax^2+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx = -\\dfrac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=-1$ and $b=4$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{4}{2(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{(-2)} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=2.$ This also represents the $x$-coordinate of the vertex. To find the $y$-coordinate of the vertex, we can substitute $x=2$ into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{2}+4x+1 \\\\  & =-(2)^{2}+4(2)+1 \\\\  & =-4+8+1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is at $(2,5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082944 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14837" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082944 #edb/ref 1071 "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=0.25x^2+kx+2$ is $x=-6.$ Find the value of $k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082944 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dad0da4b-af03-507c-9549-6f5963783da6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082944 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, we will set our result equal to $-6.$\n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=ax^2+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx = -\\dfrac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=0.25$ and $b=k$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{k}{2(0.25)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{0.5} \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-6,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2k & =-6 \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186560993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186561017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186561024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186561065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186082942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083186 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "205ecbfe-49fd-559f-a4e7-a36900f1d9c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186560972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186561003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186561032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083187 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186561041 #edb/