785519ffe9cb4333adcd602a733659d0447c37f61a.png)\n\nThe vertex of the parabola lies on the axis of symmetry, so $x=1$ also represents the $x$-coordinate of the vertex. To find the $y$-coordinate of the vertex, we can substitute $x=1$ into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3{x}^{2}-6x+1 \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}-6(1)+1 \\\\  & =3-6+1 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is at $(1,-2).$\n\n![](images/a3/a391338ffb2bddd2a58b836e328c574d348215c518b27d9886ca11a21674943a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084524 #edb/ref 1065 9241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084524 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "bfd0e6a4-644a-50b6-91df-852343ebd41e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084524 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539521 #edb/ref 1080 "(3,26)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539521 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539521 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1546d0b3-484a-554f-a971-19b0784fdf0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539526 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539526 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539526 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "171eba40-f441-599d-bfb0-408b5950a3c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539583 #edb/ref 1080 "(-3,-118)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539583 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539583 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "388620da-b528-5628-804b-351a30e184bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539678 #edb/ref 1080 "(3,-118)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539678 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539678 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7727e947-2e9c-5fb6-9177-9b23822a088a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539738 #edb/ref 1080 "(-6,-10)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539738 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539738 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9cddc5f1-bf50-5346-a250-f95ea0170398" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539800